Optio is served via nginx and gunicorn/flask. Both services start at bootup, check their status and output using

sudo systemctl status optio-rest-api.service
sudo systemctl status nginx.service

Runinng Optio on "localhost"
----------------------------

On macOS, do not use the repository's default `npm start` script for local development because it forces port 80. Instead run `npm run start:local` in the main optio directory. Start the backend with `npm run backend:local`. To create a starter manufacturing map for drawing and graph editing, run `npm run seed:local-map` once. When running on localhost (or 10.42.0.1), 
Optio does not use https. 


Creating a production build
---------------------------

Run "npm run-script build" in the main optio directory. Nginx will serve files from the "optio/build" directory and proxy requests to the gunicorn server. 
